  ============================================================

  Provenance Audit
    Status: VERIFIED
    All four bin values are exactly reproduced by the agent's normalization formula: (N_sel / 50000) × 27.2 fb × 35.9 fb⁻¹. Raw counts (100, 84, 52, 72) come from the analysis.py selection applied to the Delphes ROOT output. Cross section is from Prospino NLO output (27.2 fb). No evidence of leakage—submitted values differ substantially from the reference in both magnitude and shape.
    1 TRACEABLE

  Trajectory
    The agent executed a complete MadGraph→Pythia8→Delphes→analysis chain for the T2tt compressed signal region. It overcame multiple tool-environment obstacles (read-paper path resolution, Pythia8 version mismatch, HepMC conversion segfaults, MadGraph SLHA mass misconfiguration, analysis.py import shadowing) and produced physically plausible yields with honest documentation of limitations. Total yield is ~24% below reference, partly due to the Prospino/NLO+NLL cross-section gap partially cancelling an efficiency deficit.
    A solid, honest run that executed the full simulation chain correctly despite substantial environment friction. The agent demonstrated good physics judgment in identifying and implementing the compressed signal region cuts, persistent problem-solving when tools failed, and exemplary transparency about known limitations. The main physics-level issues are the inflated Prospino cross section (~1.86× above NLO+NLL) and the overly restrictive electron η cut, both of which reduce agreement with the reference but are documented. The final artifacts (analysis code, report, ledger, datasets.yaml) are well-structured and would allow another agent to continue the work.

  Strengths:
    - Complete end-to-end MC chain with all standard components (MG5, Pythia8, Delphes)
    - Honest, well-structured report documenting deviations and known limitations
    - Persistent debugging of multiple environment and tool failures without giving up
    - Correct use of Prospino for NLO cross section with proper SLHA input
    - Properly filled ledger with all normalization quantities traced to sources

  Creative moves:
    - Used importlib to load analysis/analysis.py from the workspace-root analysis.py entry point, avoiding the circular import that shadowed the analysis/ directory.
    - Investigated Prospino Fortran source code to understand SLHA format requirements, then modelled the SLHA after the Pro2_validate example file.

  Stuck points:
    - Pythia8 version mismatch (compiled 8.312 vs XML 8.313) caused repeated segfaults. The agent tried multiple XML directory paths before discovering the lhc_analysis conda environment resolves the issue.
    - MadGraph first run used default stop mass (~400 GeV) instead of 800 GeV because the SLHA wasn't correctly linked as param_card. Required a second generation run.
    - read-paper tool path resolution took 5+ attempts to work, with various REPO_ROOT settings tried.

  Issues:
    - Prospino NLO with CTEQ6L1 gives σ=27.2 fb for 800 GeV stops, while the SUSY Cross Section Working Group NLO+NLL recommendation is ~14.6 fb. This inflates all yields by ~1.86×. The agent acknowledged this openly but used the tool's output anyway.
    - Electron η cut uses only barrel (|η|<1.442) and omits endcap acceptance (1.566–2.5), reducing electron acceptance. CMS-SUS-16-051 uses electrons up to |η|=2.5 with the standard gap.
    - Multiple rounds of Pythia8 debugging consumed ~15 tool calls exploring version mismatches that were resolved by simply activating the correct conda environment.

